date: 2023-01-01
excerpt: >-
  Nothing matters, so why not enjoy it?
---

> Every new discovery is just a reminder that we are all small and stupid.

Nothing matters so what's the point? Everything Everywhere All At Once tackles nihilism in a way no film ever has before it. In a seemingly endless multiverse, it may feel like life is meaningless. No matter what action you take, it may feel like you will never put a dent in the world. Everything Everywhere All At Once, however, turns this ideology on its head.

If nothing matters, why not enjoy the time you have? Make new friends, tell your crush you love them, take that new job offer. Why not? What makes life meaningful is the recognition that because there is no inherent meaning, all things and moments are equally meaningful. Doing laundry and taxes is an inconsequential task, but its meaningful because the people we share the task with are worth it.

Nothing matters, so why not enjoy it?
